  "date": "2026-09-26",
  "subject": "Separate compiler preparation from ordinary source-edit feedback",
  "claim": "Ordinary development and Project 4 builds require a prepared compiler and do not reconstruct it implicitly. Explicit host-specific checkpoint selection decouples application/library builds from current compiler source; it is not current-source compiler verification. The small Windows edit loop takes 2828 then 2581 ms including execution; the Foundation Option/Result loop takes 3186 then 3100 ms. Every measured compilation created new analysis and WVB cache entries and execution observed the expected changed result.",
